        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_42_02_02",
          "sessionID": "ses_42",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_42_02",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Not quite — CI doesn't run on your laptop at all. GitHub Actions spins up a fresh virtual machine (a \"runner\") in the cloud, checks out your branch there, installs dependencies from scratch, and runs the test command in that clean environment. It has none of your local state — no node_modules you forgot to reinstall, no local env vars, no local database. That's actually the point of CI: it catches things that only work \"on your machine.\""
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_42_02_03",
          "sessionID": "ses_42",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_42_02",
          "type": "step-finish",
