      "parts": [
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_42_08_01",
          "sessionID": "ses_42",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_42_08",
          "type": "step-start"
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_42_08_02",
          "sessionID": "ses_42",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_42_08",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Not on its own — `.gitignore` only tells git which *new, currently-untracked* files to ignore. Since `node_modules` is already tracked, git keeps tracking every file in it regardless of what `.gitignore` says. You need to explicitly untrack it: `git rm -r --cached node_modules` (this only removes it from git's index, not your disk), then commit. After that, the `.gitignore` entry will keep it from being re-added."
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_42_08_03",
          "sessionID": "ses_42",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_42_08",
          "type": "step-finish",
